//! [Phase 5, P0.3] EIP-8298 (SETCODEFROM, simulated) in the connector. Generated by
//! impl/harness/phase5/make_p503_tests.py from the harness file below; only the `p503_` test is run.
//! [lifecycle Level 0 connector proof, gate G2-mock part 2] The UNMODIFIED kms-worker at v0.13.8 checks
//! user-decryption requests against the Level 0 ACL **v0.4.1** (account retirement, `retireAccount()`),
//! deployed on a local Anvil node in place of the base ACL v0.4.0.
//!
//! Test-only file. It reuses the baseline real-chain harness (`setup/host.rs`: `AnvilAcl`,
//! `init_host_chains_acl_contracts_anvil`; `setup/db.rs`: external Postgres) and adds:
//! - the Level 0 ACL implementation, loaded from a forge artifact (`LIFECYCLE_L0_ACL_ARTIFACT`) and
//!   deployed with Zama's own flow (`ERC1967Proxy(EmptyUUPSProxyACL)` then
//!   `upgradeToAndCall(ACL, initializeFromEmptyProxy())`);
//! - retirement by the real `retireAccount()` (EOAs) or by the dApp contract itself (`DappStub.retireSelf`);
//! - one fresh worker (fresh gateway/KMS mocks) per request, the ACL and the DB persisting across the
//!   requests of a test, so the same request can be sent before and after a retirement;
//! - a NEUTRAL gateway mock: every request is given what a forward needs (the coprocessor S3 bucket URL is
//!   cached by the connector's process-global cache after the first forwarded request of the test, and
//!   `max_attempts` copies of the gateway tx are queued), so only the connector's own checks can stop it;
//! - the connector's host-chain URL carries the request label as path, so the JSON-RPC recorder
//!   attributes every ACL call to the request that made it.
//!
//! Environment (set by `/srv/lifecycle/scripts/run_level0.sh`):
//! - `LIFECYCLE_ANVIL_URL`, `LIFECYCLE_HOST_RPC_URL`, `LIFECYCLE_HOST_CHAIN_ID`, `LIFECYCLE_SOL_OUT`
//!   (as in `acl_real_chain.rs`);
//! - `LIFECYCLE_L0_ACL_ARTIFACT`: Level 0 ACL artifact (bytecode + deployedBytecode);
//! - `LIFECYCLE_PG_ADMIN_URL` (+ `PGPASSFILE`): external Postgres, see `setup/db.rs`.
